"""
@title IDutchAuction
@author Curve Finance
@license MIT
@notice Minimal Dutch auction ABI compatible with a subset of Yearn Auction:
        want/available/price/getAmountNeeded/take.
@dev Only these selectors from Yearn Auction (yearn/
     tokenized-strategy-periphery, src/Auctions/Auction.sol) are implemented.
     available/price/getAmountNeeded also accept an optional evaluation
     timestamp (Vyper default arguments export both selectors); the two-arg
     getAmountNeeded matches Yearn's timestamp overload by ABI. The rest of
     Yearn's surface is absent — namely the getAmountNeeded(address) overload,
     the shortened take overloads, price(address,uint256), and the
     isActive/kicked/auctions views; Yearn tooling relying on them will not
     work unchanged. price() here is a WAD-scaled (1e18) unit price over raw
     token amounts and differs from Yearn's decimal-normalized price for sell
     tokens with non-18 decimals: integrators MUST quote with
     getAmountNeeded() instead of multiplying price(). Yearn's code is
     AGPL-3.0: only the selectors and their intended semantics were copied,
     the implementation behind this interface is independent.
"""


@external
@view
def want() -> address:
    ...


@external
@view
def available(_from: address, _ts: uint256 = ...) -> uint256:
    ...


@external
@view
def price(_from: address, _ts: uint256 = ...) -> uint256:
    ...


@external
@view
def getAmountNeeded(_from: address, amountToTake: uint256, _ts: uint256 = ...) -> uint256:
    ...


@external
def take(
    _from: address,
    maxAmount: uint256,
    takerReceiver: address,
    data: Bytes[8192],
) -> uint256:
    ...
